course: dictionary
lesson: 2404
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Custody is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «The suspect was taken into custody.» The police are holding the suspect, so custody here means being held by the police.
explain: «His mum has custody.» Family words give the clue here. Custody can mean the legal right and duty to look after a child, especially after parents separate. A court may decide this, or the parents may share it.
explain: Custody can also mean careful keeping of something valuable. «The museum has custody of the paintings.» The museum and the paintings are clues: the museum looks after them safely. Try swapping in care, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Custody means being kept, or being looked after, by someone.
fact: «In custody» means held by the police or in prison, usually while waiting to go to court.
fact: «Joint custody» means two parents share the right and duty to look after a child.
fact: «Protective custody» means keeping a prisoner alone for their own safety.
fact: Where a child lives is a grown-up decision. A child should not have to choose between parents, and a mediator or a family court can help the parents agree.
exercise: «The suspect was taken into custody.» What does custody mean here? | Being kept in a museum | Being given a prize | *Being held by the police | Being on holiday
exercise: «The museum has custody of the paintings.» What does custody mean here? | A legal right to look after a child | *Careful keeping of something valuable | Being held in prison | Being painted by an artist
exercise: Which phrase means that two parents share the right to look after a child? | safe custody | in custody | police custody | *joint custody
test: «His mum has custody.» What does custody mean in this sentence? | A famous painting | *The legal right and duty to look after a child | A holiday | A cell in a police station
test: «Protective custody» means keeping a prisoner alone for what reason? | *For their own safety | To let them go home | To punish them more | To make them famous
exam: After the divorce, a court decided which parent would have custody of the children. What does custody mean here? | Being given a prize | *The legal right and duty to look after a child | Careful keeping of a valuable object | Being held by the police
